from pathlib import Path
import json

here = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
def count(name):
    data = json.loads((here / name).read_text())
    assert data['passed'], name
    return len(data['checks'])
native, package, editor = (count(n) for n in ['checks.json', 'package-checks.json', 'editor-checks.json'])
html = '''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>The Void — Point Zero and a floor editor</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#eeebe4;color:#252a30;font:18px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:40px 28px 80px}h1{font-size:clamp(36px,6vw,68px);line-height:1.05;max-width:950px;margin:16px 0 24px}h2{font-size:28px;margin:38px 0 14px}p{max-width:850px}a{color:#63304c}nav{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px}.lede{font-size:24px}figure{margin:22px 0}img{width:100%;display:block;border-radius:6px}figcaption{font-size:14px;color:#535a63;margin-top:8px}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16px}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-top:1px solid #c8c4bd;padding:13px}th{width:22%}.card{background:#fff9;border-radius:8px;padding:22px;margin:20px 0}.button{padding:12px 18px;background:#282e37;color:white;border-radius:5px;text-decoration:none}code{font-size:.88em}li{margin:8px 0}@media(max-width:760px){.pair{display:block}main{padding:24px 16px}th{width:30%}}</style>
<main><div class="eyebrow">The Void · 18 October 2026 · working prototype</div>
<h1>Point Zero, on the roof.<br>A fixed tower with editable rooms.</h1>
<p class="lede">The running counter is already there when you arrive. The origin stays at world zero. A common electrical route leads across the slab to four stations; two shafts lead down.</p>
<nav><a class="button" href="http://localhost:3003/editor/void">Open the floor editor</a><a href="#museum">Native Godot views</a><a href="#checks">Checks</a></nav>
<figure id="museum"><img src="point-zero.png" alt="Point Zero's live counter and pink origin on the open concrete rooftop"><figcaption>Actual Godot viewport. The existing counter and origin scenes are installed in The Void. The instruction board has been moved clear of the counter.</figcaption></figure>
<table><tr><th>Before</th><td>A playable roof and two lower floors: open shafts, columns, temporary landings and empty attachment markers.</td></tr><tr><th>Now</th><td>Point Zero on the roof, four floor stations on each level, four facing directions, editable walls and a catalyst-responsive patch on Floor 01.</td></tr><tr><th>Kept</th><td>The fixed frame, both descent routes, fatal falls and last-floor checkpoints. The museum's original Point_Zero map and its texts remain intact.</td></tr></table>
<div class="pair"><figure><img src="counter.png" alt="The running counter connected to a floor supply socket"><figcaption>The real frame counter. Its supply enters behind the display.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="origin.png" alt="The existing origin marker at world zero inside a raised wire cage"><figcaption>The origin is a fixed reference at (0,0,0), separate from the four artifact stations.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>One content file, two views</h2><p>The editor and Godot read <a href="../../../../commons/void/rooms.json">rooms.json</a>. Each floor keeps its map reference, title, walls, artifact placements and settings, and the cells that may answer a catalyst hit. <a href="../../../../commons/void/layout.json">layout.json</a> holds the permanent tower frame. The <a href="../../../../commons/void/rooms.schema.json">JSON schema</a> and shared validator check saves before they reach the game.</p>
<figure><img src="editor.jpg" alt="The Void editor with a plan, station placement controls and map reference"><figcaption>Four stations: NW, NE, SW, SE. Choose a station, an artifact and a facing. Search accesses the project registry. Draw a wall with two clicks, or select catalyst cells in the central patch.</figcaption></figure>
<p>Saving keeps a backup and rejects a stale edit if the file changed elsewhere. Reload The Void to use saved changes. The existing web editor and Godot MapToolEditor both link to this floor editor.</p>
<h2>Only the impacted cell changes</h2><div class="pair"><figure><img src="impact-before.png" alt="Eight dark floor panels before a catalyst impact"><figcaption>Before: the authored panels remain still. Walking and elapsed time do not change them.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="impact-after.png" alt="One floor panel raised and coloured pink after a catalyst shot"><figcaption>After a real projectile collision: one panel rises. Its collider changes with its mesh. Repeated hits cycle its height; the structural slab beneath it stays intact.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>Test it</h2><div class="card"><p><strong>VR:</strong> launch the project and choose <strong>The Void</strong>. Left stick moves; right stick turns. Right A or right trigger jumps. <strong>Left trigger fires the catalyst.</strong> Right B retries the saved floor; left Y returns to the roof; left X returns to the menu.</p><p><strong>Desktop:</strong> open <code>commons/void/void.tscn</code> and F6. WASD, mouse, Space; <strong>C fires</strong>. R retries, T returns to the roof, M returns to the menu. Aim at the dark panels on Floor 01.</p></div>
<h2 id="checks">What was verified</h2><p><strong>NATIVE</strong> native Godot / Jolt checks, <strong>PACKAGE</strong> packaged-build checks and <strong>EDITOR</strong> schema/API checks passed. The package uses Android exclusions in a Windows PCK; it is not a headset or APK test.</p><ul><li>Existing artifacts load; the counter advances; world zero stays at zero.</li><li>Editor scale, facing and wall height reach the runtime. Duplicate stations, non-cardinal angles, blocked checkpoints and protected cells are rejected.</li><li>A real catalyst shot raises one panel, leaving its neighbour unchanged. Left-trigger input fires once per press.</li><li>Both shafts remain open. Desktop and the real XRTools body, driven by synthetic tracking, complete the descent and recover to checkpoints.</li><li>The browser was used to save/reload scale and facing, draw/remove a wall, and enable/remove a catalyst cell.</li></ul><p><a href="checks.json">Native assertions</a> · <a href="package-checks.json">Package assertions</a> · <a href="editor-checks.json">Editor assertions</a> · <a href="receipt.json">Runtime receipt</a></p>
<h2>What comes next</h2><p>The common supply is visible infrastructure; power and power failure are not simulated yet. We should define what “off” means for each artifact, check footprint and hand reach as exhibits are added, and decide which artifact changes should survive death. Currently catalyst panels keep their state during a visit and reset when the scene reloads.</p><p>The full registry is available for placement, but that does not certify every artifact's fit or interaction in this minimal VR rig. Grab/flight are still outside this prototype. Physical headset testing remains necessary.</p><p>Whole-app TypeScript checking still reports existing errors elsewhere in the encyclopedia; the new editor and API files have no reported type errors.</p></main></html>'''
html=html.replace('NATIVE',str(native)).replace('PACKAGE',str(package)).replace('EDITOR',str(editor))
(here/'index.html').write_text(html,encoding='utf-8')
print(f'Published: {native} native, {package} package, {editor} editor checks')
